$\begin{align}
\blueE{20\%} \text{ of }\maroonD{90} &= \blueE{\dfrac{20}{100}} \cdot \maroonD{90}\\\\
&=\blueE{\dfrac{1}{5}} \cdot \maroonD{90}
\end{align}$

$\blueE{20\%}$ of a number *always* equals $\blueE{\dfrac{1}{5}}$ of the number.

What is $\blueE{\dfrac{1}{5}}$ of $\maroonD{90}$?
